there has recently been a lot of talk  about apple working on a virtual reality  headset  which could be used for vr gaming but in  my opinion  i don't think a lot of people are gonna  buy it and i'll explain why in just a  minute  i'm also gonna be discussing my  experience with the oculus quest  2 vr headset which is the best  mainstream gaming headset so far  but before i get into that let's go  through the history of apple vr headset  leaks and rumors  way back in 2008 over 12 years ago  apple was reportedly researching a  laser-based head-mounted display  but since the tech was so old back then  it relied on using an  ipod and a compact laser engine that  attaches to your  belt so this shows that apple's been  interested in head mounted displays  for many years now way later in 2013  apple was granted a patent for a  goggle-like video headset  designed to allow users to view media  while on the go  there was even an image of a cable  connecting an ipod to the headset  and that's because the patent was  originally filed in 2008  then in 2015 apple hired on a small team  working on augmented reality projects  with the goal of creating a wearable  device  only two months later apple acquired the  augmented reality startup  mittayo which focused on building  virtual reality experiences  and then in 2016 apple hired doug  bowman a lead virtual reality researcher  who actually worked on a bunch of  different headsets like the oculus rift  microsoft hololens and even google glass  and just a few days later it was  revealed that apple had a secret team  working on a virtual reality headset  with hundreds of employees  exploring both vr and augmented reality  and apparently they had already built  prototype vr headsets  which were inspired by the oculus rift  and that was way back in 2016.  two years later the vr developer studio  named servios  stated that apple is putting a lot of  effort and passion  into virtual reality including vr gaming  a little bit later it was revealed that  the youtuber mark rober  was actually helping apple work on an  anti-motion sickness vr technology  headset  for use in the future autonomous apple  car  the point was that the car would be able  to drive itself so you can kick back and  enjoy some media  using a vr headset while you drive to  work  which honestly seems like a dream come  true if it actually ends up working out  but unfortunately  mark rober confirmed that he left that  position  in 2019 and a year later apple filed a  new patent showing that they're still  interested in this vr headset technology  meant to battle motion sickness by  creating an immersive world  with a virtual environment and now  finally in 2021  we just got a bunch of specific details  on what to expect from apple's vr  headset  so let's get right into the new leaks  and rumors a couple of weeks back  mark german reported that apple's first  virtual reality headset  will be a pricey niche precursor  to a more ambitious augmented reality  product it'll display an  all-encompassing 3d digital environment  for gaming  watching video and communicating with  apple launching it  as soon as 2022 apparently the price  will be far more expensive  than those from rivals with apple not  really expecting to sell that many of  them  so it'll be a high-end niche product  like the mac pro  the report also says that apple plans to  pack in higher resolution displays  in the headset than those in current vr  offerings  which might explain the high price and  it's also supposed to get  much more powerful chips than even the  m1 chip in recent max  mark even says that apple could include  a fan in the device pointing to a ton of  graphics performance being built in  now on the other hand apple is also  working on augmented reality glasses  codenamed n421 which could be released  as early as 2023 and apple was also said  to be working on  hand tracking features like typing on a  keyboard in mid-air  and just two days ago we got another  report from the china times  about apple's vr headset releasing in  the first quarter of 2022  with lidar technology which is already  in use in apple's iphone 12 pro  and their ipad pro the report says that  the design of the headset will look very  similar  to that of other vr headsets jpmorgan  believes that this headset will be  targeted at the top end of the consumer  market  being more expensive than other vr  headsets  with the device's materials also  exceeding 500  which shows that apple could be charging  big bucks potentially over a thousand  dollars for this headset  and just yesterday we got even more  details  and this is where it starts to get very  exciting but also  very disappointing the information  reported that apple's upcoming vr  headset  is said to feature dual 8k displays  yes not one but dual 8k  displays this is insane because the  current most popular oculus quest 2  headset  features dual 2k displays and in my  experience  it actually looks pretty good and i'll  get to that in just a minute  running dual ak displays means that you  would need a ton of graphics performance  or some kind of upscaling technology so  it would make sense why it would come  with a built-in fan  from that previous rumor the headset  will apparently compact with more than a  dozen cameras  for tracking hand movements with some of  the cameras tracking eye movements  within the headset as well and  apparently the cameras will record the  environment in front of you  and pass it on through the display so  you can get a mixed  reality effect the information said that  they actually viewed a late stage  prototype  which showed a sleek curved visor  attached to the face  by a mesh material and with swappable  headbands  so i wonder if it's the same kind of  mesh used in the airpods max  headphones apparently you can also swap  out the headband  based on what you need like having  spatial audio technology  or additional battery life there will  also be multiple ways to control the  headset  including a thimble-like device worn on  a person's finger  or of course eye and hand movements  and there could be a dial on the side of  the visor which will probably be a crown  like on the apple watch  now here comes the crazy part they said  that apple internally discussed  pricing the headset around a massive  three thousand dollars which absolutely  blows my mind  but apparently microsoft's hollow lens  two  is also very expensive at thirty five  hundred dollars  so it might try to compete with that  that microsoft headset is a very niche  product  meant for high-end professional use so  it kind of seems like apple's headset  might be going the same route if this is  true but based on all the features that  i just mentioned  like having over 12 cameras and a dual  8k  displays it makes sense why it could be  so expensive  and that right there is the main reason  why most people will  not be buying apple's vr headset because  even if apple  significantly drops the price from that  three thousand dollar estimate  it's still going to be way too expensive  for most consumers  even at a thousand dollars it's overkill  for most people  because the current best vr headset the  oculus  quest 2 is only 300 on amazon  and most people should honestly just buy  that instead  it basically offers a complete vr  headset in one package  with a comfortable headband built-in  speakers and  decent displays the two and a half hour  battery life is just enough for a long  vr gaming session and you can use a  battery bank if you need more  there's a wide variety of available  games like population one  which i really enjoyed since it features  a battle royale style map  and really nice gameplay but my favorite  game was  beat saber and i was impressed with how  well the controls and tracking worked  so i've got to say that the oculus quest  2 is the first  vr headset which is actually great and  at its 300  purchase price it's affordable to most  people  being cheaper than a ps5 or an xbox  series x  now i know that apple's vr headset will  be the mother of all vr products  and it might even revolutionize virtual  reality  but i think if it's priced at anywhere  near two or three thousand dollars  i don't think most people are gonna be  interested so there you guys have it  hopefully you guys enjoyed this video  and if you did  tap the like button below click the  circle above to subscribe  check out one of those two videos right  over there thank you guys for watching  and we'll see you in  the next one
 

